# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test interaction between unique checks and multi-region features.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Given a FK reference to a parent table which is unique on a subset of the FK
# columns, it is possible to infer a functional dependency on the child table.
# Currently, this optimization is only applied to RBR tables and results in
# FDs of the form (parent_id --> crdb_region). This results in two improvements:
#
# 1) If the child has a UNIQUE constraint on (parent_id), we can avoid expensive
#    cross-region unique checks, and instead only check the region supplied by
#    the input row.
#
# 2) If the child has a UNIQUE constraint on (crdb_region, parent_id), we can
#    prove that (parent_id) alone is a key, potentially enabling other
#    optimization rules to fire.
#
